# CODEOWNERS — review gate for protected and high-blast-radius paths
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# Work on this repo is increasingly done by AI agents (Claude, Codex,
# Antigravity) opening PRs from `claude/`, `codex/`, and `antigravity/`
# branches. Agents are good at scoped, well-specified changes and bad at
# knowing which changes are irreversible. This file makes the owner a
# required reviewer on the paths where a mistake is expensive, slow to
# detect, or impossible to undo.
#
# The protected domains below come from `AGENTS.md` and
# `.claude/skills/vsa-change-control/`. That skill is authoritative; this
# file is the mechanical enforcement of a subset of it. If the two ever
# disagree, AGENTS.md wins and this file is wrong.
#
# ⚠️  READ THIS BEFORE RELYING ON IT: this file is currently ADVISORY ONLY.
#
# CODEOWNERS only *requests* review. It becomes an actual merge gate via
# branch protection ("Require review from Code Owners") — and on a PRIVATE
# repository, branch protection and rulesets require a paid plan (GitHub Pro
# for a personal account; Team for an organization). On GitHub Free they are
# public-repo only.
#
# So right now this file documents ownership and auto-requests review. It
# does NOT stop anyone — human or AI agent — from merging a change to any
# path below. Treat review of these paths as a convention you enforce by
# hand, not something the platform enforces for you.
#
# It becomes a real gate, with no edits needed here, if either:
#   - the repository is made public (branch protection is then free), or
#   - the account moves to a plan that includes it.
#
# Verify current state:
#   gh api repos/hhavynn/vsa-website/branches/main/protection
# A 404 means unprotected — this file is advisory.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default — everything else needs no specific owner
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# (intentionally no global rule; unowned paths stay reviewable by anyone)

